* The flying fox (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script and our own
* art from art/flyingfox.py and basket3d.py). Run by openc2e after
* the world loads (Additions folder); made anew each load.
*
* A woven basket rides a rope from the plank deck west of the stone arch
* (floor 840) down past the small waterfall to the bamboo scaffold by the
* desert lift (floor 1285), and back (owner, 2026-11-10: a way between the
* two). The rope falls 1 px for each px west, so the basket's top-left is
* always at (x, 4513 - x): x 3767 at the deck stop, 3322 at the scaffold.
*
* 1. The scaffold's landing: room 61 (the scaffold, floor 1285, solid over
*    the room below) reaches to x 3512 (was 3368), past the basket's stop,
*    with room for its caller at the end; room 250, the open air east of it,
*    starts there. ROOM takes all of a room's data, so each room's own values
*    are passed back.
room 61 2904 840 3512 1285 room 61 4 room 61 5 room 61 6 room 61 7 room 61 8 room 61 9 room 61 12 room 61 13 room 61 14 room 61 15 room 61 16 room 61 17 room 61 19
room 250 3512 840 3768 1285 room 250 4 room 250 5 room 250 6 room 250 7 room 250 8 room 250 9 room 250 12 room 250 13 room 250 14 room 250 15 room 250 16 room 250 17 room 250 19
*
* 2. The line (zffl): the rope, the green cane post and brace it is tied to
*    on the deck, the stub post at the scaffold, the landing's planks on two
*    braced posts. Behind creatures.
enum 2 3 243 kill targ next
inst new: simp zffl 1 0 -24 0 setv cls2 2 3 243 setv attr 0 mvto 3355 690 slow
*
* 3. The basket (vehicle 3 2 150, sprite zffb): part 0 its back (inside, far
*    rim and cords; plane 1400), part 1 its front (near wall, rim, cords and
*    the pulley on the rope; plane 1600, click-through). Riders are drawn at
*    1401, between them (CABP); the cabin is the basket's floor (94 px below
*    its top) between its walls. Like the game's lifts, activate 1 sends it
*    down (to the scaffold) and activate 2 up (to the deck), gathering the
*    creatures in it on the way and setting them down on arrival; a caller at
*    each end brings it there. OV00 the stop it is at or left (0 the deck, 1
*    the scaffold), OV01 the stop it is going to, OV02 the state (0 waiting,
*    1 boarding, 2 riding, 3 arriving), OV03 its speed (px a tick, along x),
*    OV04 a count of ticks.
enum 3 2 150 kill targ next
inst
new: vhcl zffb 2 0
setv cls2 3 2 150
new: part 0 0 0 0 1400
new: part 1 0 0 1 1600
tran 1 1
part 0
cabp 1401
cabn 20 0 126 94
setv attr 4
bhvr 0 0
setv ov00 0 setv ov01 0 setv ov02 0 setv ov03 0 setv ov04 0
mvto 3767 746
tick 1
slow

* down to the scaffold
scrp 3 2 150 1
  doif ov02 eq 0
    doif ov00 eq 0
      setv ov01 1 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0
    endi
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
* up to the deck
scrp 3 2 150 2
  doif ov02 eq 0
    doif ov00 eq 1
      setv ov01 0 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0
    endi
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm
scrp 3 2 150 0
  setv actv 0
endm

* every tick (all at once: INST). Boarding: a short pause, then the
* creatures at the basket are gathered (GPAS). Riding: speeds up by 1 px a
* tick to 10 and brakes as evenly into the stop (the speed from which
* braking by 1 a tick stops in the distance left: the whole-number square
* root of 2 x distance, at least 1), keeping to the rope. Arriving: a short
* pause, then the riders are set down (DPAS).
scrp 3 2 150 9
  inst
  doif ov02 eq 1
    addv ov04 1
    doif ov04 ge 8
      gpas
      setv ov02 2 setv ov03 0 setv ov04 0
      snde shut
    endi
    stop
  endi
  doif ov02 eq 3
    addv ov04 1
    doif ov04 ge 6
      dpas
      setv ov02 0 setv ov04 0
    endi
    stop
  endi
  doif ov02 eq 2
    setv var0 3767
    doif ov01 eq 1 setv var0 3322 endi
    setv var1 var0 subv var1 posl
    setv var2 var1
    doif var2 lt 0 negv var2 endi
    addv ov03 1
    doif ov03 gt 10 setv ov03 10 endi
    setv var7 var2 mulv var7 2
    setv var3 0
    reps 31
      setv var6 var3 addv var6 1 mulv var6 var6
      doif var6 le var7 addv var3 1 endi
    repe
    doif var3 lt 1 setv var3 1 endi
    doif ov03 gt var3 setv ov03 var3 endi
    doif var2 gt ov03
      setv var4 ov03
      doif var1 lt 0 negv var4 endi
      setv var5 posl addv var5 var4
      setv var6 4513 subv var6 var5
      mvto var5 var6
    else
      setv var6 4513 subv var6 var0
      mvto var0 var6
      setv ov00 ov01 setv ov02 3 setv ov03 0 setv ov04 0
      snde shut
    endi
  endi
endm

* 4. The callers, a pole caller at each end (the game's own picture, cbt2,
*    from the player's installed copy, as the arch lift's; owner,
*    2026-11-10: the same at both ends): at the deck right of the post's
*    brace (2 2 222), at the scaffold on the landing's end (2 2 221). Each
*    brings the basket to its own stop.
enum 2 2 221 kill targ next
enum 2 2 222 kill targ next
inst new: simp cbt2 2 0 5000 0 setv cls2 2 2 222 setv attr 196 bhvr 1 0 pose 0 mvto 3934 740 slow
inst new: simp cbt2 2 0 5000 0 setv cls2 2 2 221 setv attr 196 bhvr 1 0 pose 0 mvto 3476 1185 slow
*
* 5. The leafy plant by the scaffold (2 3 5 at 3359/1140, plane 0) hid the
*    rope's lower stretch and the landing (owner, 2026-11-10): it goes behind
*    them (plane -30; the line is at -24). PLNE is openc2e's in C2.
enum 2 3 5 doif posl eq 3359 doif post eq 1140 plne -30 endi endi next
scrp 2 2 222 1
  pose 1 snde ding
  enum 3 2 150 doif ov02 eq 0 doif ov00 ne 0 setv ov01 0 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0 endi endi next
  wait 30 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 222 2
  pose 1 snde ding
  enum 3 2 150 doif ov02 eq 0 doif ov00 ne 0 setv ov01 0 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0 endi endi next
  wait 30 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 221 1
  pose 1 snde ding
  enum 3 2 150 doif ov02 eq 0 doif ov00 ne 1 setv ov01 1 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0 endi endi next
  wait 30 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
scrp 2 2 221 2
  pose 1 snde ding
  enum 3 2 150 doif ov02 eq 0 doif ov00 ne 1 setv ov01 1 setv ov02 1 setv ov04 0 endi endi next
  wait 30 pose 0 setv actv 0
endm
*
* 6. The scaffold beside the landing (owner, 2026-11-10): the jump-pad toy
*    there (2 13 1, a world-file object at 3137/1237; the world's five other
*    jump pads stay) is taken out, and the desert lift's capsule caller (2 2
*    1, at 3304/1205, crowded against the basket's stop) moved into its place.
*    The caller stays linked to its lift (the world file links them as
*    objects).
enum 2 13 1 doif posl gt 3100 doif posl lt 3200 doif post gt 1200 doif post lt 1290 kill targ endi endi endi endi next
enum 2 2 1 doif posl eq 3304 doif post eq 1205 mvto 3141 1205 endi endi next
